            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for hide-and-seek, then the Gujarati for a puzzle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: શિલ્પ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શિલ્પ — śilp — \"a sculpture\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મંદિરમાં પથ્થરનાં ઘણાં સુંદર શિલ્પ છે. mandirmā̃ paththarnā̃ ghaṇā̃ sundar śilp che. There are many beautiful stone sculptures in the temple."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શિલ્પ (śilp) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit śilpa, \"an art, a craft\" (Monier-Williams); in Gujarati it is a work of sculpture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
